<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Livonian Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1198–1290</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades">Northern Crusades</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Livonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was the conquest and Christianisation of present-day Latvia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> by German crusaders, chiefly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Riga and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a>, with Danish forces in northern Estonia, from about 1198 to 1290. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Livs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgalians">Latgalians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a>, Curonians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semigallians">Semigallians</a> were subdued in turn. The conquered lands formed the confederation known as Terra Mariana or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/livonian-crusade.jpg" alt="Livonian Crusade" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LivoniaKnight.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
